{"title":"Career roadmap — System Administrator","role":"System Administrator","summary":"A System Administrator (SysAdmin) manages an organisation's servers, operating systems, user accounts, networks, storage, backups, security controls, monitoring, and IT infrastructure. For a BCA student specialising in Cloud Computing / DevOps, this role can be an excellent foundation for progressing into Cloud Engineering, DevOps, SRE, Infrastructure Engineering, and Cybersecurity.","facts":{"Current degree":"BCA (Bachelor of Computer Applications)","Course":"BCA – Cloud Computing / DevOps"},"about":[{"label":"Core principle","text":"Modern system administration is no longer only about maintaining physical servers. The strongest SysAdmins combine Linux + Windows + networking + cloud + automation + security + monitoring."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus","What to build"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Junior System Administrator"},{"text":"Linux, Windows Server, networking, scripting, virtualization"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"System Administrator / Cloud Administrator"},{"text":"Cloud, IAM, monitoring, automation, infrastructure management"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Senior SysAdmin / Infrastructure Engineer / DevOps Engineer"},{"text":"IaC, containers, Kubernetes, CI/CD, reliability"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Infrastructure Architect / SRE Lead / Cloud Architect"},{"text":"Enterprise architecture, automation, resilience, governance"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Operating systems + networking"},{"type":"h","text":"Linux"},{"type":"p","text":"Become comfortable with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ubuntu"},{"text":"Rocky Linux / RHEL concepts"},{"text":"Filesystem"},{"text":"Users and groups"},{"text":"Permissions"},{"text":"Processes"},{"text":"Services"},{"text":"Pack